<!-- htpd section {"n":2,"id":"sections/0002-revision-history","number":null,"level":1,"pages":[2,2,2],"parent":"document"} -->
## [S2] Revision history

Path: Revision history - page 2

<!-- page 2 -->

Rev 1.2 adds the thermal derating rule and corrects the contactor ratings.

Rev 1.1 adds Appendix A.

<!-- htpd section {"n":3,"id":"sections/0003-1-introduction","number":"1","level":1,"pages":[2,2,2],"parent":"document"} -->
## [S3] 1 Introduction

Path: 1 Introduction - page 2

<!-- page 2 -->

The controller supervises the power stage and the vehicle interface. It samples the bus voltage, the output current and three temperature sensors every 10 ms and reports the values over the internal CAN bus. All limits in this chapter apply over the full operating temperature range unless a different condition is stated in the table.

<!-- htpd section {"n":4,"id":"sections/0004-1-1-scope","number":"1.1","level":2,"pages":[2,2,2],"parent":"sections/0003-1-introduction"} -->
## [S4] 1.1 Scope

Path: 1 Introduction > 1.1 Scope - page 2

<!-- page 2 -->

This manual describes the 60 kW DC charger controller board, hardware revision C. It covers electrical limits, the charging sequence and the register map.

<!-- htpd section {"n":5,"id":"sections/0005-1-2-terms","number":"1.2","level":2,"pages":[2,2,2],"parent":"sections/0003-1-introduction"} -->
## [S5] 1.2 Terms

Path: 1 Introduction > 1.2 Terms - page 2

<!-- page 2 -->

• EVSE: electric vehicle supply equipment.

• CCS: combined charging system.

The term inter-rupt latency means the time from the fault to the opening command.

<!-- htpd section {"n":6,"id":"sections/0006-2-electrical-characteristics","number":"2","level":1,"pages":[2,2,3],"parent":"document"} -->
## [S6] 2 Electrical characteristics

Path: 2 Electrical characteristics - page 2

<!-- page 2 -->

The controller supervises the power stage and the vehicle interface. It samples the bus voltage, the output current and three temperature sensors every 10 ms and reports the values over the internal CAN bus. All limits in this chapter apply over the full operating temperature range unless a different condition is stated in the table.

<!-- htpd section {"n":7,"id":"sections/0007-2-1-supply","number":"2.1","level":2,"pages":[2,2,2],"parent":"sections/0006-2-electrical-characteristics"} -->
## [S7] 2.1 Supply

Path: 2 Electrical characteristics > 2.1 Supply - page 2

<!-- page 2 -->

The logic supply is 3.3 V. The contactor coil supply is 12 V.

<!-- htpd section {"n":8,"id":"sections/0008-2-1-1-limits","number":"2.1.1","level":3,"pages":[2,2,2],"parent":"sections/0007-2-1-supply"} -->
## [S8] 2.1.1 Limits

Path: 2 Electrical characteristics > 2.1 Supply > 2.1.1 Limits - page 2

<!-- page 2 -->

```text
Parameter | Min | Typ | Max | Unit
Logic supply voltage | 3.0 | 3.3 | 3.6 | V
Coil supply voltage | 10.8 | 12.0 | 13.2 | V
Bus voltage | 200 | 400 | 480 | V
Output current | 0 |  | 200 | A
```

<!-- htpd section {"n":9,"id":"sections/0009-2-2-contactor","number":"2.2","level":2,"pages":[2,3,3],"parent":"sections/0006-2-electrical-characteristics"} -->
## [S9] 2.2 Contactor

Path: 2 Electrical characteristics > 2.2 Contactor - pages 2-3

<!-- page 2 -->

The output contactor is rated for 200 A. It is controlled by the control board, which receives its commands from the MCU.

<!-- page 3 -->

